        <xsd:documentation>This element contains WBI's 2 to 4-letter weather word classification, 9AM to 9PM local time.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - WX_2_9A_9P
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - WBI 2-DIGIT PREDOMINATE WEATHER (9A - 9P)


</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="WBINineAMToNinePMWeatherText" type="xsd:string">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains WBI's full-length weather description, 9AM to 9PM local time.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - WX_TEXT_9A_9P
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - PREDOMINATE WEATHER TEXT  (9A - 9P)</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TenAMToFourPMMaxTemperature" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the maximum temperature in degrees Fahrenehit between the hours of 10PM - 4AM, local time.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - MAX_TEMP_10P_4A
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - Maximum temperature between the hours of 10PM - 4AM, local tim

</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TenAMToFourPMMinTemperature" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the minimum temperature in degrees Fahrenehit between the hours of 10PM - 4AM, local time
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - MIN_TEMP_10P_4A
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - Minimum temperature between the hours of 10PM - 4AM, local time</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SeasonFirstDaySnowGreaterHalfInchIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a "1" for  the first day  observing 0.50" snowfall (at the weather station defined by the 4-letter code), all other days are marked by "0".  The snow season goes from August 1st to July 31st.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - FIRST_SNOW_1
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name -
</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SeasonFirstDaySnowGreaterOneInchIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a "1" for  the first day  observing  1.0" snowfall (at the weather station defined by the 4-letter code), all other days are marked by "0". The snow season goes from August 1st to July 31st.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - FIRST_SNOW_2
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SeasonFirstDaySnowGreaterTwoInchIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a "1" for  the first day observing &gt;2.0" snowfall (at the weather station defined by the 4-letter code), all other days are marked by "0".  The snow season goes from August 1st to July 31st.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - FIRST_SNOW_3
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SnowLocalStormReportIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>Thius element contains a binary ="1", with any LSR (public) Report from any NWS office, or, any finalized report from SPC, listing any snow amount; assume calendar day of report is day of observation; Limited by 35-miles to weather station code, or, zip code center.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - SNOW_LSR
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SnowLocalStormReportMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the max Amount of all LSR (public) Reports from any NWS office, or, any finalized report from SPC, listing any snow amount; assume calendar day of report is day of observation.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - SNOW_LSR_AMT
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SnowLocalStormReportMeasureTypeCode" type="xsd:string">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the type of measurement used in SNOW LSR Report, M = MEASURED, E = ESTIMATED; default to E if unknown
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - SNOW_LSR_MEA_T
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - 
</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SnowLocalStormReportDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the general distance to observation (miles; report location to weather station).
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - SNOW_LSR_DIS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - Distance from station of report in miles:</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="BlizzardIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a "1" to indicate blizzard conditions.
It is consider a blizzard  if the Average Wind Speed &gt; 15 MPH during Snow hours, plus the Average Visibility &lt; 1.5 Miles during Snow hours; AND calendar day  Snow &gt; 4"; or there is a National Weather Service  "BZ" Advisory, Watch, or Warning.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - BLIZZD
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="RainLocalStormReportIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a binary ="1", with any LSR (public) Report from any NWS office, or, any finalized report from SPC, listing any RAIN amount; assume calendar day of report is day of observation; Limited by 35-miles to weather station code, or, zip code center.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - 
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - RAIN_LSR</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="RainLocalStormReportMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the max amount of all LSR (public) Reports from any NWS office, or, any finalized report from SPC, listing any RAIN amount; assume calendar day of report is day of observation.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - RAIN_LSR_AMT
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="RainLocalStormReportMeasureTypeCode" type="xsd:string">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the type of measurement used in RAIN LSR Report . 
 Valid values include:
	'M' = MEASURED
	'E' = ESTIMATED or default to E if unknown.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - RAIN_LSR_MEA_T
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="RainLocalStormReportDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the general distance to observation (miles; report location to weather station).
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - RAIN_LSR_DIST
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - Distance from station of report in miles</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SeasonFirstDayFreezeIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element indicates the first day observing 32°F or colder at the weather station with a binary "1", all other days are marked by "0.  The Freeze season goes from  August  1st- July 31st.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - FIRST_FREEZE_1
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FloodingMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a WeatherBank, Inc. calculated field that, based on proprietary logic and local rainfall reports, determines the actual or forecasted occurrence of FLOODING.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - 
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - FLOOD1</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FloodFourDayIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a numeric indicator is set to 1 if the 4-day running precipitation amounts exceed regional defined limits.  
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - FLOOD2
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HailIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to 1 if there is any occurance of hail within the Zip Code. 
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - HAILB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HailSizeMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is a measure of the size of Hail, in inches, observed or forecast at the location.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - HAILS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HailDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the distance in miles of hail observed to current Zip Code center.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - HAILD
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TornadoIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>The element indicates the occurrence of a Tornado or NWS Tornado Warning inside Zip Code.  A BINARY ="1"
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - TORB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - 
</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TornadoDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the distance of Tornado to current Zip Code center.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - TORD
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="ExtremeWindSpeedIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to 1 when there is an occurrence of Extreme Wind Speed (&gt;65 mph) anywhere within the ZIP Code.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - EXT_WINDB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="ExtremeWindSpeedMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the actual or estimated Extreme Wind Speed, in miles per hour, within the ZIP Code.  It defaults to 65 mph if unknown.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - EXT_WIND_SPD
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - 

</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="ExtremeWindSpeedDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is the distance in miles to the Extreme Wind Event, to ZIP CODE Center or weather station code.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - EXT_WIND_DIS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HurricaneIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a binary value is set to 1 if there is a zip code inside the NHC (NOAA) impact area of a Tropical Storm or Hurricane force wind speed, actual or forcasted through 7 days.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - HURRB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HurricaneIntensityCode" type="xsd:string">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element accompanies HURRB, a predefined VALUE of TS/Hurricane INTENSITY; actual or forecasted; B = Tropical Depression (Wind Speeds  39- 56 MPH); A = Tropical Storm Event(Wind Speeds  58- 74 MPH); 1 = Hurricane, Category 1 Event (Wind Speeds  74- 95 MPH); 2 = Hurricane, Category 2 Event (Wind Speeds  96-110 MPH); 3 = Hurricane, Category 3 Event (Wind Speeds 111-130 MPH); 4 = Hurricane, Category 4 Event (Wind Speeds 131-155 MPH); 5 = Hurricane, Category 5 Event (Wind Speeds &gt; 155 MPH)
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - HURRI
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - 
</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TropicalSystemIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element indicates any zip code inside a circled area extending from a tropical system (TD or TS) of 150-miles, having wind speeds (observed or predicted) within 25-38 mph;  with WBI's FLOOD=1; caused by any/all these triggers: 1) rain observed or predicted exceeding the 99.99-percentile amount; 2) NWS FLOOD WARNING issued; 3) NWS FLASH FLOOD WARNING issued.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - TROP1
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="AverageDayHeatIndexMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the average daily Heat Index temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, calculated during daytime; i.e. from Sunrise to Sunset.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name - AVG_HI_DAY_SS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - The average Heat Index Temp°F during daytime (Sunrise to Sunset)</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="AverageNightHeatIndexMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the average daily Heat Index temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, during nighttime, defined as Sunset to Sunrise. 
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -AVG_HI_NIGHT_SS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - The average Heat Index Temp°F during nighttime (Sunset to Sunrise)</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="TenAMToFourPMAverageHeatIndexMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the average daily Heat Index temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, during nighttime, defined as10PM to 4AM local time.  
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -AVG_HI_NIGHT_10P_4A
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - The average Heat Index Temp°F during nighttime (10PM to 4AM local time) </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="Average24HourHeatIndexMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is the average Heat Index Temp°F across calendar day (24-hours) 
This is the average daily Heat Index temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, calculated based on the calendar day (24 hours).</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="PowerOutageRiskCode" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element ranks the likelihood of a power outage due to the risk of severe thundrstorm and/or tornado activity.  The values range from 0 if no conditions satisfying POUT are met, up through 3, indicating a high risk. </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="PowerOutageWindRiskIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to 1 when there is a potential fora power outage due to extreme winds (wind speeds &gt;55 mph), either observed or forecasted, and/or there is a risk of a severe thunderstorm or tornado.</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="IceIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to one for any occurrence of ICE, FREEZING RAIN, FREEZING DRIZZLE, FREEZING FOG, ICE FOG, ICE PELLETS observed or forecasted.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -ICEB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="IceAmountCode" type="xsd:integer">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element value varies from 1 (lowest) to 3 (highest) based on either a weather station observation or NWS NDFD forecast of  ICE, FREEZING RAIN, FREEZING DRIZZLE, FREEZING FOG, ICE FOG, ICE PELLETS. 
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -ICEA
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - Amount of ICE, actual or forecasted
Values: 
1 - Weather station observation, if amount is unknown 
	Station observation or NWS NDFD forecast, TRACE to 0.10"
2 -  Weather station observation or NWS NDFD forecast, 0.11"  to 0.25"
3 - Weather station observation or NWS NDFD forecast, &gt;0.25"
	NWS issues ICE STORM WARNING, ICE ACCRETION WARNING, FREEZING RAIN WARNING, ICE PELLET WARNING, HEAVY ICE PELLET WARNINGS
	NWS WINTER STORM ADVISORY, WATCH or WARNING mentioning ICE
	NWS issues ICE STORM WATCH, ICE ACCRETION WATCH, FREEZING RAIN WATCH, ICE PELLET WATCH, HEAVY ICE PELLET WATCH, regardless of amounts
	




</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SleetIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to '1' if there is any occurrence of SLEET reported at any weather station code, or, by ANY LSR or in any finalized SPC report. 
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -SLEETB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - The occurrence of SLEET  a binary 1 for sleet
</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SleetAmountCode" type="xsd:integer">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a code value set based on the occurrence of SLEET : 1=TRACE to 0.25", 2=0.26" to 0.50", or 3=&gt;0.50"
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -SLEETA
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HeatIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a value that is set to 1 when there is an occurrence of  any NWS HEAT ADVISORY, HEAT WATCH or HEAT WARNING.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -HEATB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="HeatAmountCode" type="xsd:integer">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains a value range of 1 to 3 (lowest to highest), based on the hotter of two inputs: WBI MAX HEAT INDEX or NWS HEAT ADVISORY.   
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -HEATA
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FlashFloodWarningIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to 1 if The National Weather Service has issued a FLASH FLOOD WARNING for the area inside this zip code.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -FFW
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FloodIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains an indicator set to 1 if the National Weather Service has issued a FLOOD WARNING, or a COASTAL FLOOD WARNING, or an AREAL FLOOD WARNING for the area inside this zip code.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -FLD
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FireIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains satellite detected wildfire, within 250-miles, of at least 20-dections by satellite over the past 7-days (number of fires exceeding 20-count within ½-mile)
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -FIRE
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="FireDangerRatingCode" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the danger ranking per WBI's proprietary Fire Danger Rating Model. Values range from 0 (Low Danger) to 5 (Extreme danger) based primarily on environmental factors. 
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -FIRE_DANGER
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="EarthquakeIndicator" type="xsd:boolean">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is set to 1 when there has been an occurrence of an Earthquake measuring 5.50 or greater, within the reporting ZIP CODE.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -EQB
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="EarthquakeDistanceMeasure" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element contains the measure of the distance of the Earthquake from the current ZIP CODE center when there is an earthquake of 5.50 or greater within the zip code.
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -EQ_DIS
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="NumberOfHoursVisibilityLessHalfMiles" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation> This element is a measure of the total Number of hours in a calendar day, with VISIBILITY &lt; 0.50-mile
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -VIS1
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="NumbersOfHoursVisibilityHalfToOneMile" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is a measure of the total Number of hours in a calendar day, with VISIBILITY &gt;= 0.50 mils and  &lt; 1.0-mile
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -VIS2
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="NumberofHoursVisibilityOneToTwoHalfMiles" type="xsd:decimal">
				<xsd:annotation>
          
        <xsd:documentation>This element is a measure of the total Number of hours in a calendar day with VISIBILITY &gt;= 1.0 mile and &lt; 2.0-miles
AccuWeather Vendor Data Field Name -VIS3
AccuWeather Vendor Full Name - </xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>

		</xsd:sequence>
	</xsd:complexType>
</xsd:schema>